ct fabric together and after this  was like explosion i was crocheting  gigantic installation right away  crocheting is a process of making fabric  with one continuous loop  i travel around the world every time i  go all my projects somehow relates to  the community i'm working with  our pink house is the project i created  in avesta in sweden  this town accepted a lot of refugees  from syria and ukraine  in india we were crocheting a new skin  for homeless shelter  probably most people know my work  because of the wall street bull i  appreciate pink camouflage as the  respond to the recent market crash that  happened 2008.  [Music]  currently i'm working on a project i  love across the usa  i want to create a mural in every state  that portrays women that change american  history  i always create squares or rectangles  sometimes and then when i have enough  pieces i crochet piece by piece together  with the help of the local people who  want to be part of this action so first  i touch this i go through this  and then just go on a live and install  it  people want to be part of something  and i love seeing that hunger  that  people have to create something so  positive not just the image but the  power that every single loop is made by  somebody's hand  [Music]  complex  [Music]  is  [Music]  [Music]  is  [Music]  nosotros  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  okay  [Music]  foreign  [Music]  in saskatoon saskatchewan you'll find  four senior citizens making socks  lots and lots of socks socks by bob have  knitted 11  662  as of today  that's pairs of socks which means socks  by bob has knitted 23  324 individual socks 8.8 miles of socks  and they're all for charity  the man responsible for all these socks  is none other than bob rutherford  [Music]  enter bob's knitting machines  these super powered knitting machines go  at 90 turns per second that's pretty  fast  but what makes these machines special  are that they're self-made  i'm an experimenter i just build things  and 